 "review": {"identity": "Devin SWE-2/swe2-max-1", "method": "Acceptance suite run locally with `retail,gpu,audio` (CS_GAME_DIR, CS_ENGINE_IMAGE): the owner's own command `cs --cs-path $CS_GAME_DIR --mission M01 --smoke-seconds 45 --capture-dir private/evidence/PARITY-M01-PLAYER-VIEW` drove the same windowed composition the owner plays on this machine's GPU — through the launch cinematic — and wrote real framebuffer PNGs plus report.json with its scripted checks passing. A second, no-teleport run (`--smoke-no-teleport`) flew the measured start pose continuously — never moving the player (`player_teleported:false`, `placements:[]`) — and wrote the parity frames at the owner-capture seconds: `frame_01500_flight_25s.png` and `frame_04200_flight_70s.png`, the frames `orig25.png` and `orig70.png` are compared against at the same simulated time, plus the post-sample `flight` frame the run already took. `cs_xtask parity` aligned the two pairs into `private/parity-m01/sheet/` (sheet.png, report.json, report.md) for side-by-side reading; the report states 'visual comparison needed' and no numeric metric is a parity verdict. The retail test composes M01 headless and asserts the integrated view at once: the capture-fitted chase eye resolved astern-and-above the one player body, the measured `prop1` blur disc drawn on it while the engine runs, and both measured `wing_flare` quads bound to the player actor's `leftwingdamage`/`rightwingdamage` nodes, reading `Unknown` and `Hidden` — the intact presentation. The runs are automated, never `human_play`, and no original executable ran. This harness derives every field from the recorded log, production discovery of $CS_GAME_DIR, the smokes' reports and the hashes of those artifacts. LIMITS: the chase preset is a designed capture fit (the original's offset, FOV and smoothing stay unknown), the player has no damage graph so orig70.png's burning presentation is exercised by the accept_ tests only, and the sprite trail and gauge wiring are follow-ups #1700/#1701 — scale and orientation matching is the designed fit's claim, not a measured original value. Validated with tools/validate_evidence.py (structure and artifact hashes, exit 0); --require-pass reports the recorded follow-up unknowns as unresolved issues, which stand as this task's honest limitations rather than being emptied to pass the gate."},
